PERFORMANCE WORK STATEMENT (PWS) 

1.  Contract or Task Order Title.  Virtual Reality Training for a Gas Turbine Generator


2.  Background.  

Pearl Harbor Naval Shipyard & Intermediate Maintenance Facility (PHNSY&IMF) is developing its workforce in surface ship and submarine repair and maintenance. Elevating technical competence through training directly enhances shipyard capability, operational efficiency, and safety.

3.  Objectives: 

PHNSY&IMF requires a Contractor to develop and build a Virtual Reality (VR) training system leveraging commercial-off-the-shelf (COTS) technology for the use of a gas turbine generator. The Contractor shall deliver this system, complete with instructional animations to maximize and improve operational readiness and maintenance capabilities across all platforms. The VR animations must be user-driven and built according to specifications in the PWS.


4.  Scope.  

The Contractor shall provide all management, labor, transportation, tools, and equipment for the delivery of the VR hardware and VR software training system solution identified in the PWS. The delivery of the software training system must be completed by Close of Business (COB) November 1, 2027. Annual software and hardware maintenance for the system is required. 

5.  Performance Requirements.  

TASK: VR Software Development (Standalone Training)

The Contractor shall:

Ensure all new software development uses modern software development methodologies (e.g., agile, Development, Security, and Operations (DevSecOps)) for rapid delivery of standardized, reliable, integrated and secure mission capabilities.

Gather system requirements, develop the architecture, design, integrate and test software modules and field the software for use by the PHNSY&IMF user community. Contractor shall:

Provide at least one (1) visit to PHNSY&IMF to facilitate software development.

Ensure VR software technical requirements are approved by and for Government use;

Ensure VR software training system (developed instructions and part of software subscription) is compatible and compliant with equipment authorized for use by PHNSY&IMF, Code 109;

Ensure VR software system has software protections for Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) level data;

Ensure any photo, video, and three-dimensional (3D) scanning, if required to develop the training system, has compliant labeling and marking to expedite review process with PHNSY&IMF, Code 1120;

Include Department of Navy (DoN) specifications for the Gas Turbine Generator (450-480VAC);

Include the Auxiliary fuel tank environment and the Gas Turbine Generator environment in the software training system at minimum;

Include onsite procedures for use of the Gas Turbine Generator, including onsite procedure document and environment capture;

Include step-by-step procedures with real-time misstep detection for the Gas Turbine Generator, which consists of:

Safety procedures;

Set-up procedures;

Pre-operational procedures;

Manual startup procedures;

Operational procedures;

Manual shutdown procedures;

Hand signals pertinent to the Gas Turbine Generator;

Include interactive gauges and indicators;

Include anomaly and troubleshooting scenarios for advanced proficiency;

Include multi-user capabilities for 4-5 simultaneous users in shared VR sessions.

Develop and build the VR software training system based on system requirements for use by the PHNSY&IMF user community. VR training shall include:

VR software requirements that are approved by and for Government use;

VR software (developed instructions and part of software subscription) that is compatible and compliant with equipment authorized for use by PHNSY&IMF, Code 109;

Software protections for CUI level data;

Photo and video with compliant labeling and marking approved by PHNSY&IMF, Code 1120;

3D virtual model of the Gas Turbine Generator;

DoN specifications for the Gas Turbine Generator (450-480VAC);

Auxiliary fuel tank environment and Gas Turbine Generator environment;

Onsite procedures for use of the Gas Turbine Generator; 

Step-by-step procedures with real-time misstep detection for the Gas Turbine Generator. Training instructions shall include:

Safety procedures;

Set-up procedures;

Pre-operational procedures;

Manual startup procedures;

Operational procedures;

Manual shutdown procedures;

Hand signals pertinent to the Gas Turbine Generator

Interactive gauges and indicators;

Anomaly and troubleshooting scenarios for advanced proficiency;

The delivery of the software content must be completed by COB November 1, 2027. 



Ensure that the software/application is free from all computer viruses, worms, time-outs, time bombs, back doors, disabling devices and other harmful or malicious code intended to or may damage, disrupt, inconvenience or permit access to the Software user's or another's software, hardware, networks, data or information.   Notify the Government within 30 minutes of malicious activity embedded within one of the contractual deliverables. 

Establish formal software development, code control and build processes for major and minor (patches) releases and full integration.

Track all revisions in the VR software training system;

Provide software configuration management of modifications.

Ensure the VR training system can be installed and operated by following these steps:


Validate VR training system and its instructions to verify accuracy and completeness in accordance with PWS requirements.

Modify VR training system and instructions upon Government request.

The Contractor shall provide a report detailing the nature of the services performed; upgrade modifications and other pertinent information concerning the condition of the equipment to Government.  The Contractor shall submit the report within 10 business days after delivery of the software training system on November 1, 2027.

Option Year 1: Contractor shall provide 

A Government Cloud solution that includes environment setup, hosting, and networking of the VR training approved by Government. 

A collaborative training workshop for multi-users and capabilities for 4-5 simultaneous users in shared VR sessions compliant with Information Leve 5 (IL5) environment approved by Government.

TASK: VR Hardware

The Contractor shall:

Deliver five (5) Trade Agreements Act (TAA)-compliant HTC Vive Focus Vision VR headsets compatible with the VR training software solution provided by the Contractor. Hardware has 12-month manufacturer warranty.

Headsets shall have separate login accounts for admins and general users;

Ensure headsets are in working condition during delivery handoff to the Government;

Include all necessary VR headset accessories, such as dongles, hard carrying cases, and similar accessories that are required for the VR headset to operate with the training solution and to protect headset from physical damage to the Government;

Provide Government help with the setup, use, care, and operation of the headset.

Option Year 2: Contractor shall provide annual maintenance for VR headsets, as well as software and content updates.

Option Year 2: Contractor shall provide annual IL5 GovCloud hosting and networking support.

